{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' <original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/references/aristotle-cli.md && rg -n -i -C 3 'P40|BicommutantNormalTransport|closeout|bicommutant normal' PROGRESS.md README.md reviews aristotle_responses aristotle_tasks 2>/dev/null | head -400 && find aristotle_responses -maxdepth 2 -mindepth 1 -type d -printf '%p\\\\n' | sort\"","aggregated_output":"# Aristotle CLI reference\n\n## Setup\n\n- Install: `uv tool install aristotlelib`\n- Verify: `aristotle --version`\n- Authenticate: set `ARISTOTLE_API_KEY` in the shell environment, or use the skill wrapper `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh`.\n\nIf the key is stored near the end of `~/.bashrc`, noninteractive commands may not see it because many `.bashrc` files contain:\n\n```bash\ncase $- in\n    *i*) ;;\n      *) return;;\nesac\n```\n\nIn that case, do not rely on `source ~/.bashrc`. Use the wrapper, which reads a literal `export ARISTOTLE_API_KEY=...` assignment without printing it:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh formalize input.md\n```\n\n## Core commands\n\nSubmit a Lean project for sorry filling or proof search:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh submit \"Fill in all sorries\" --project-dir ./my-lean-project --wait\n```\n\nFormalize a TeX or paper source:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh formalize paper.tex --wait --destination output.tar.gz\n```\n\nList recent jobs:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh list --limit 10\n```\n\nDownload a completed job:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh download <project-id> --destination result.tar.gz\n```\n\nPass the key directly for one command only:\n\n```bash\naristotle submit \"My prompt\" --api-key \"$ARISTOTLE_API_KEY\" --project-dir ./my-lean-project --wait\n```\n\n## Recommended project loop\n\n1. Inspect the Lean project locally.\n2. Run the narrowest local build or test that exercises the target files.\n3. Submit a focused Aristotle prompt against the project directory.\n4. Wait for the run if the expected result is a concrete patch.\n5. Download or inspect the produced artifact.\n6. Rebuild locally and repeat with a tighter prompt if needed.\n\n## Prompt shape\n\nKeep prompts short and file-bound. Good prompts mention:\n\n- the exact project directory\n- the theorem or file to work on\n- whether to fill `sorry`s, formalize a statement, or debug a failing proof\n- what counts as a useful partial result\n\nAvoid vague prompts such as \"improve this project\" unless the scope is intentionally broad.\nreviews/P37-algebraic-limit-operator-representation-closeout.md:1:# P37 closeout review — algebraic-limit operator representation\nreviews/P37-algebraic-limit-operator-representation-closeout.md-2-\nreviews/P37-algebraic-limit-operator-representation-closeout.md-3-## Decision\nreviews/P37-algebraic-limit-operator-representation-closeout.md-4-\n--\nreviews/P37-algebraic-limit-operator-representation-closeout.md-90-  reviewed integration;\nreviews/P37-algebraic-limit-operator-representation-closeout.md-91-- `aristotle_responses/P37-algebraic-limit-operator-representation.tar.gz` and\nreviews/P37-algebraic-limit-operator-representation-closeout.md-92-  its extracted quarantine snapshot, preserving the raw remote response;\nreviews/P37-algebraic-limit-operator-representation-closeout.md:93:- this closeout review.\nreviews/P37-algebraic-limit-operator-representation-closeout.md-94-\nreviews/P37-algebraic-limit-operator-representation-closeout.md-95-All pre-existing modified and untracked files were preserved. No manuscript\nreviews/P37-algebraic-limit-operator-representation-closeout.md-96-file was modified, and no commit or push was made.\n--\nreviews/P38-concrete-quasilocal-cstar-model-closeout.md:1